WEBVTT

00:21.521 --> 00:25.025
3 YEARS AGO

00:25.108 --> 00:25.942
JAPANESE FORCES

00:26.026 --> 00:26.901
JOSEON FORCES

00:27.402 --> 00:28.653
SANGJU

00:37.203 --> 00:39.539
This will bring the dead back to life?

00:41.750 --> 00:43.084
This plant?

00:44.586 --> 00:46.254
Yes, it will, my lord.

00:48.339 --> 00:49.841
The plant's essence...

00:50.759 --> 00:53.511
when injected in the glabella
of the deceased,

00:54.345 --> 00:58.266
will revive the body as a monster
that hungers for the flesh of the living.

00:58.683 --> 01:01.102
However, if the corpse is decayed...

01:02.145 --> 01:04.939
or if the center of the brain
has already been damaged,

01:05.899 --> 01:07.650
resurrection is impossible.

01:12.322 --> 01:14.491
[foreboding music]

01:37.722 --> 01:39.641
[soldier 1] The Japanese
have us surrounded.

01:39.724 --> 01:42.018
Sangju is all that stands
in Gyeongsang Province.

01:42.102 --> 01:44.312
I heard the Japanese have reached
the Unpo Wetland.

01:44.729 --> 01:47.107
Well, if that's true,
then Sangju is done for.

01:47.190 --> 01:48.149
Oh, wait.

01:48.233 --> 01:49.859
- Does that mean we're--
- [shushes]

01:53.571 --> 01:54.614
[gasps]

01:59.994 --> 02:01.496
[crow squawking]

02:06.876 --> 02:09.003
[foreboding music]

02:47.834 --> 02:49.085
[squawks]

03:03.224 --> 03:06.352
[crows squawking]

03:19.240 --> 03:20.783
BASED ON THE KINGDOM OF THE GODS BY YLAB

03:20.867 --> 03:22.535
[opening theme music]

04:19.175 --> 04:20.385
[snarls]

04:56.879 --> 04:59.424
[distant snarling]

05:07.515 --> 05:09.684
[suspenseful music]

05:18.401 --> 05:21.821
[snarling]

05:29.579 --> 05:31.414
[tense music]

05:41.799 --> 05:43.551
How are they out in daylight?

05:52.518 --> 05:54.437
Prepare weapons, take your positions.

05:54.520 --> 05:55.438
[blows horn]

06:03.446 --> 06:04.739
It won't catch fire!

06:23.549 --> 06:24.425
[screeches]

06:45.446 --> 06:46.280
[screams]

06:50.118 --> 06:51.202
[man screams]

06:57.917 --> 06:58.918
Burn them now!

07:03.881 --> 07:04.757
Get to the raft!

07:07.051 --> 07:09.804
- Get the rest out of the water! Hurry!
- Go! Go!

07:10.388 --> 07:11.848
Come on! Push!

07:29.115 --> 07:30.158
[shrieks]

07:30.241 --> 07:31.826
That's it! Push!

07:44.046 --> 07:46.841
Run! Go, run!

07:51.512 --> 07:53.097
[tense music]

08:23.920 --> 08:25.254
Yah! Yah!

08:25.338 --> 08:27.381
THE CITADEL OF SANGJU

08:27.465 --> 08:29.425
The infected are coming! They're awake!

08:29.509 --> 08:30.885
[man] Master!

08:31.802 --> 08:34.222
The monsters are at Byeongseong Stream!

08:35.306 --> 08:36.974
BYEONGSEONG STREAM

08:37.058 --> 08:38.392
[men screaming]

08:41.437 --> 08:43.105
[tense music]

08:47.026 --> 08:48.653
We can't hold out much longer, sir!

08:49.278 --> 08:50.655
Use the cannons! Fire!

09:09.966 --> 09:11.300
[pants]

09:17.557 --> 09:20.351
- [soldier 1] Bring more arrows! Hurry!
- [soldier 2] Here! Take it!

09:51.591 --> 09:52.883
Push them back!

09:52.967 --> 09:54.719
If you let them break through,
we're all dead!

09:54.802 --> 09:55.720
[soldier 1] Yes, sir!

10:13.613 --> 10:14.572
[yells in pain]

10:20.161 --> 10:21.954
- [gasping]
- [yells]

10:35.176 --> 10:36.010
Sir!

10:36.594 --> 10:38.554
We cannot fight them any longer!

10:39.263 --> 10:40.514
Your Highness, we have to flee.

10:41.849 --> 10:44.143
[tense music]

10:59.533 --> 11:00.534
THE CITADEL OF SANGJU

11:00.618 --> 11:02.244
That's the citadel. They are falling back.

11:02.828 --> 11:04.580
Ready the rope ladders, now!

11:12.171 --> 11:14.632
[suspenseful music]

11:47.039 --> 11:47.915
[whimpers]

11:49.250 --> 11:51.085
- Oh, no.
- [men gasp in fright]

11:52.628 --> 11:54.588
[all gasp in fright]

11:56.424 --> 11:57.466
[man 1] He's been bit!

11:58.008 --> 11:58.843
No...

11:59.885 --> 12:00.970
It's a small bite.

12:02.179 --> 12:03.264
It will be okay.

12:03.347 --> 12:05.182
[pants]

12:06.434 --> 12:07.435
Please.

12:07.768 --> 12:08.978
Please.

12:09.061 --> 12:10.479
No, please!

12:15.067 --> 12:15.985
[yells]

12:18.362 --> 12:19.822
Please! Help!

12:20.448 --> 12:21.699
Help! Help!

12:33.252 --> 12:34.670
[man 3] What do we do now?

12:35.379 --> 12:36.922
Sangju's our only option.

12:37.298 --> 12:38.924
If we can make it, there's a path.

12:39.341 --> 12:41.177
What if those monsters are there, too?

12:41.260 --> 12:42.845
Do you want to stay here and freeze?

12:50.644 --> 12:53.981
BYEONGSEONG STREAM

12:56.650 --> 12:58.652
THE CITADEL OF SANGJU

12:59.069 --> 13:02.364
[indistinct shouting]

13:04.158 --> 13:05.618
- Help us!
- Hurry up!

13:05.701 --> 13:06.660
Grab the ladder!

13:06.744 --> 13:08.662
- The infected are here!
- [gasps]

13:09.580 --> 13:11.832
[snarling]

13:14.293 --> 13:16.712
[men screaming]

13:22.468 --> 13:24.553
[suspenseful music]

13:27.348 --> 13:29.099
[panting]

13:30.810 --> 13:32.978
[Deok-soong] The infected
got through Byeongseong Stream.

13:35.105 --> 13:38.150
Your Highness, I know of a passageway.

13:38.234 --> 13:40.778
Built during the war,
on the north branch of the stream.

13:42.321 --> 13:44.532
Let's hurry. Protect His Highness!

13:45.282 --> 13:46.367
We must go now!

13:48.035 --> 13:49.995
[tense music]

13:54.083 --> 13:57.127
HONGCHI GATE

14:21.402 --> 14:22.653
It's locked! We're trapped!

14:22.736 --> 14:24.280
[man straining]

14:25.698 --> 14:26.740
Damn it!

14:26.824 --> 14:28.200
Form a blockade now!

14:28.284 --> 14:31.537
[indistinct shouting]

14:38.210 --> 14:40.421
[snarling]

14:43.632 --> 14:44.550
They're coming!

14:44.633 --> 14:45.718
They're here!

14:46.385 --> 14:49.013
- [man 2] Get in formation!
- [man 3] Hurry! Hurry! Get ready!

14:57.479 --> 14:59.315
[yelling]

15:23.130 --> 15:24.423
[screeches]

15:43.901 --> 15:45.235
Make way!

15:51.700 --> 15:53.285
You must hurry!

15:57.748 --> 15:58.582
Out of the way!

16:09.677 --> 16:10.970
Sir! Your Highness!

16:11.053 --> 16:12.388
The gate is open!

16:12.471 --> 16:15.140
- Prepare, Your Highness!
- Prepare to run!

16:16.976 --> 16:17.893
Your Highness!

16:17.977 --> 16:19.436
- Go!
- Go, go, go! It's open!

16:19.520 --> 16:20.437
Come on, go!

16:24.066 --> 16:25.109
[strains]

16:27.611 --> 16:29.363
- Get inside! Go!
- No!

16:30.489 --> 16:31.991
What's the matter?

16:33.575 --> 16:34.451
You can't.

16:37.788 --> 16:39.957
[foreboding music]

16:59.810 --> 17:02.312
[snarling]

17:12.740 --> 17:16.744
Guard and protect my Lord Ahn! Now go!

17:34.678 --> 17:35.929
[Mu-yeong] We must keep moving.

18:16.261 --> 18:17.471
Sorry.

19:04.226 --> 19:05.519
[man] Your Highness.

19:05.602 --> 19:08.147
[indistinct chatter]

19:08.605 --> 19:09.857
What's wrong with you?

19:12.109 --> 19:14.403
I thought Your Highness said
they retreated at daybreak.

19:16.113 --> 19:17.239
I am at a loss.

19:18.782 --> 19:20.742
They return to corpses in the sun.

19:22.703 --> 19:24.246
There must be a reason.

19:31.295 --> 19:33.297
[foreboding music]

19:34.381 --> 19:36.800
[infected snarling echoes]

19:39.094 --> 19:40.262
Why they're here...

19:43.307 --> 19:44.975
makes no difference.

20:03.452 --> 20:05.913
[foreboding music]

20:08.874 --> 20:11.501
[snarling]

20:21.261 --> 20:24.139
[grunting]

20:30.646 --> 20:32.564
[Beom-pal] Seo-bi! Seo-bi, help me!

20:33.315 --> 20:34.858
Please! Seo-bi!

20:35.442 --> 20:37.110
Seo-bi!
[grunting]

20:43.033 --> 20:44.952
[both grunting]

20:45.786 --> 20:47.788
[whimpering]

20:52.125 --> 20:54.169
[gasps, pants]

20:58.882 --> 21:00.175
[gasps]

21:01.510 --> 21:03.720
[snarling]

21:05.639 --> 21:07.683
Oh. Wait, wait. The sun is out.

21:08.517 --> 21:10.477
Why are they still moving around?

21:11.770 --> 21:15.357
It's the cold.
The resurrection plant prefers it.

21:15.440 --> 21:16.650
[pants]

21:16.733 --> 21:17.818
If they are at all alike,

21:17.901 --> 21:20.112
then sunlight
is not what they are afraid of.

21:20.904 --> 21:23.073
They only fear high temperatures.

21:23.865 --> 21:27.494
But now that it's winter,
it stays cold even with the sun.

21:27.577 --> 21:28.954
They will never cease now.

21:30.539 --> 21:31.665
[sighs]

21:44.136 --> 21:47.306
Their numbers have stayed the same
since their attack yesterday.

21:50.892 --> 21:52.019
[stammers]
So... so?

21:52.769 --> 21:55.230
That means they are
the only monsters nearby.

21:55.731 --> 21:58.066
If there were more,
they would have attacked us.

21:59.901 --> 22:02.446
Even if those are
the only monsters around here,

22:02.529 --> 22:04.698
the citadel will surely have hundreds!

22:04.781 --> 22:07.034
How do you suppose
we survive the journey back?

22:07.117 --> 22:09.369
If we go up the stream,
they should not follow.

22:09.453 --> 22:11.955
Since they cannot cross the water,
we should head up this mountain.

22:12.039 --> 22:13.999
It's far safer
than returning to the citadel.

22:16.793 --> 22:19.338
Seo... Seo-bi. Up the mountain?

22:19.421 --> 22:21.006
Where will we go?

22:22.549 --> 22:24.801
Did you not tell me once before

22:24.885 --> 22:27.471
that the Haewon Cho Clan
is able to guarantee your safety?

22:27.554 --> 22:29.222
We will go to Mungyeong Saejae.

22:29.306 --> 22:30.557
[Beom-pal gasps]

22:32.100 --> 22:33.810
Wait, Seo-bi...

22:34.644 --> 22:36.521
- [distant snarling]
- [whimpers]

22:36.605 --> 22:39.858
SUNGRYE GATE

22:41.943 --> 22:44.112
[foreboding music]

22:45.781 --> 22:48.450
[indistinct chatter]

22:53.455 --> 22:55.874
[man] I heard a rumor
that a plague is upon us.

22:55.957 --> 22:57.667
There's been sightings of ghosts.

23:00.921 --> 23:03.173
ROYAL COMMANDERY DIVISION

23:06.551 --> 23:10.305
Due to urgent matters, the Chief State
Councilor has left for Mungyeong Saejae.

23:10.680 --> 23:13.809
Now what is it that requires my absence
from the State Council?

23:13.892 --> 23:14.851
What do I have to see?

23:15.435 --> 23:17.062
This matter is of great importance.

23:17.145 --> 23:19.398
I requested your presence
to see it for yourself.

23:32.119 --> 23:33.245
All right. What is this?

23:36.164 --> 23:39.042
[commander] Last night, we found
these women outside the north gate.

23:39.626 --> 23:43.255
According to the autopsy, one of the women
had only just given birth.

23:44.840 --> 23:46.550
The baby we found with her

23:46.633 --> 23:49.428
had been strangled to death
prior to our discovery.

23:50.679 --> 23:52.139
Is the culprit detained?

23:52.639 --> 23:56.101
[commander] They said the woman uttered
something peculiar before she died.

23:56.184 --> 23:59.312
She claimed the people in her village
did this to her and her child,

23:59.771 --> 24:01.773
and that they would kill
every last one remaining.

24:01.857 --> 24:02.941
Those were her final words.

24:03.733 --> 24:05.026
Where is this village?

24:13.285 --> 24:14.119
[door closes]

24:15.662 --> 24:17.873
Outside the north gate
of Samgye-dong, Naeseonjae.

24:18.415 --> 24:20.041
"Naeseonjae"? You're sure of it?

24:20.709 --> 24:22.419
Yes, it's the private residence...

24:23.420 --> 24:25.297
and current home of the Queen's family.

24:27.382 --> 24:29.634
[crows squawking]

24:45.984 --> 24:47.986
[foreboding music]

24:50.071 --> 24:51.740
[jingling]

25:04.044 --> 25:05.462
[jingling]

25:15.847 --> 25:19.351
[woman] The Royal Commandery Division
knows about Naeseonjae.

25:20.769 --> 25:24.105
We must seek immediate assistance
from the Chief State Councilor.

25:24.189 --> 25:25.857
We cannot tell my father.

25:27.984 --> 25:29.319
We must keep this secret.

25:32.155 --> 25:33.740
My father must never know.

25:43.542 --> 25:45.502
[foreboding music]

25:49.923 --> 25:52.008
When I give birth to a prince...

25:54.386 --> 25:57.138
the Royal Commandery, nor anyone else,

26:00.141 --> 26:02.227
will not be able to challenge me.

26:06.731 --> 26:08.775
[snarls]

26:09.609 --> 26:11.361
[ominous music]

26:19.619 --> 26:21.705
Before the crescent moon sets,

26:22.205 --> 26:23.957
prepare a ritual table.

26:25.792 --> 26:26.960
That day...

26:29.379 --> 26:32.132
the goddess of childbirth
will bless you with a prince.

26:43.351 --> 26:46.896
THE WALLS OF MUNGYEONG SAEJAE

26:46.980 --> 26:49.482
[crows squawking]

27:07.459 --> 27:09.836
He had a jade ornament
of the Haewon Cho Clan,

27:09.919 --> 27:11.880
so that is why
we let him in past the gates.

27:12.589 --> 27:14.174
[gasps]
Uncle!

27:14.257 --> 27:16.092
CHEONGSUDANG

27:16.843 --> 27:18.637
[whimpers]

27:19.387 --> 27:21.348
It is I, your only nephew, Beom-pal.

27:21.890 --> 27:24.809
A strange disease spread on my first day
as magistrate in Dongnae.

27:24.893 --> 27:26.561
I barely escaped
to here with my own life.

27:27.479 --> 27:29.189
Please, grant me shelter.

27:29.981 --> 27:30.940
I see.

27:32.025 --> 27:34.819
I appointed you magistrate of Dongnae.

27:35.445 --> 27:39.991
And yet, it appears
all you've managed thus far...

27:40.950 --> 27:42.911
is protecting your pathetic life!

27:46.122 --> 27:48.917
Uncle, I'm not sure I understand.

27:49.000 --> 27:51.378
Dongnae was placed in your care.

27:53.505 --> 27:56.758
What were you doing, exactly,
while the Crown Prince...

27:58.051 --> 28:01.805
under your nose murdered the commander
of the Royal Army in Dongnae?

28:04.516 --> 28:07.185
Wait, wait. Do you mean...
that Beom-il is dead?

28:09.020 --> 28:10.188
I wasn't aware.

28:10.647 --> 28:12.315
I promise, I wasn't aware!

28:13.983 --> 28:16.027
Please believe me! I did not know!

28:17.737 --> 28:18.988
You should be grateful...

28:21.366 --> 28:23.660
that Haewon Cho blood flows within you.

28:24.619 --> 28:26.079
[whimpers]

28:26.579 --> 28:28.456
That man is Dongnae's magistrate...

28:29.457 --> 28:31.418
and Haewon Cho Clan's only heir.

28:32.836 --> 28:34.838
See that he is treated accordingly.

28:36.131 --> 28:37.507
[Hak-ju sighs]

28:38.466 --> 28:40.051
And what of the woman behind you?

28:46.057 --> 28:47.058
The thing is,

28:48.101 --> 28:50.854
she is a nurse who worked
for the physician, Dr. Lee Seung-hui.

28:50.937 --> 28:53.022
I would not be alive
if it were not for her.

28:55.525 --> 28:57.527
Dr. Lee Seung-hui, the physician?

29:00.655 --> 29:02.157
Is that true?

29:05.785 --> 29:07.120
Yes, my lord.

29:08.705 --> 29:11.374
See to it that she has
accommodations as well.

29:16.421 --> 29:18.590
[ominous music]

29:21.009 --> 29:23.678
THE CITADEL OF SANGJU

29:23.762 --> 29:26.347
[snarling]

29:34.189 --> 29:36.149
[foreboding music]

29:38.193 --> 29:39.277
[dog whimpers]

29:44.741 --> 29:47.118
- [distant snarling]
- [all gasp, whimper]

29:51.247 --> 29:53.249
[snarling, screeching]

30:13.228 --> 30:14.979
Even with careful rationing...

30:15.897 --> 30:17.607
the food will only last five more days.

30:18.733 --> 30:20.985
With this many refugees,
there's not enough.

30:23.404 --> 30:26.908
In that case, each morning,
hand out food to every last one.

30:28.785 --> 30:30.078
You're correct to ration,

30:30.912 --> 30:32.956
but the people should not starve.

30:45.176 --> 30:47.178
This is not the disease we know of.

30:48.513 --> 30:50.390
Things were not like this three years ago.

30:51.182 --> 30:52.892
They only ate flesh of humans.

30:53.434 --> 30:55.270
Bites did not lead to infection,

30:55.353 --> 30:57.522
and the infected did not rise
during sunlight.

31:00.733 --> 31:01.860
He's hiding something.

31:02.777 --> 31:04.946
Lord Cho Hak-ju knows more
about the disease.

31:05.029 --> 31:06.322
He has deceived you...

31:07.198 --> 31:08.783
and all of us, my lord.

31:14.956 --> 31:16.541
What are you trying to say?

31:19.919 --> 31:21.045
I feel...

31:22.088 --> 31:24.048
we are paying for the decision
we made back then.

31:24.507 --> 31:25.884
This is our punishment.

31:30.972 --> 31:32.181
You have regrets?

31:35.018 --> 31:36.102
My lord.

31:39.397 --> 31:41.065
I have no regrets at all.

31:41.608 --> 31:44.485
Three years ago, Sangju...

31:44.944 --> 31:46.487
and Gyeongsang were spared.

31:47.614 --> 31:49.115
If given the choice,

31:49.657 --> 31:51.659
I would not change a single act.

31:54.871 --> 31:56.122
My apologies.

31:56.998 --> 31:59.042
I have forgotten my place for the moment.

31:59.626 --> 32:02.253
I will join the others
and ensure the citadel's security.

32:25.443 --> 32:27.070
[wind whistling]

32:41.000 --> 32:41.834
Your Highness.

33:08.486 --> 33:09.737
Your Highness.

33:11.072 --> 33:13.074
I overheard Lord Ahn Hyeon...

33:14.200 --> 33:16.452
say an odd thing to one of his men.

33:17.036 --> 33:18.329
They spoke as if...

33:18.871 --> 33:21.374
they already know many things
about this disease.

33:22.792 --> 33:25.712
And it seems Lord Cho Hak-ju
is implicated as well.

33:27.880 --> 33:28.881
Your Highness.

33:29.424 --> 33:31.676
I believe it best to leave this place.

33:32.260 --> 33:33.970
I will escort you, Your Highness.

33:34.595 --> 33:36.097
You will be much safer...

33:37.140 --> 33:39.559
back through the passage
and up the north branch.

33:45.440 --> 33:47.900
Why are you sharing
this information with me?

33:50.069 --> 33:50.987
Sir?

33:58.536 --> 34:00.163
Did Cho Hak-ju command you to?

34:01.998 --> 34:02.957
Sir.

34:04.500 --> 34:06.335
Lord Ahn Hyeon told me...

34:07.128 --> 34:09.881
that the palace guards knew
I was en route to here.

34:12.717 --> 34:14.177
Was that your doing?

34:20.933 --> 34:22.018
So, then...

34:23.811 --> 34:25.897
are you trying to sow doubt between...

34:26.773 --> 34:28.566
Lord Ahn and I right now?

34:29.901 --> 34:31.110
Your Highness.

34:35.406 --> 34:37.366
You assume you cannot trust me now?

34:40.536 --> 34:42.789
I left everything, my pregnant wife,

34:44.248 --> 34:46.375
I left my family to follow you.

34:47.960 --> 34:50.463
I've come all the way
to Gyeongsang for you.

34:53.841 --> 34:56.260
And even now, you still do not trust me?

35:04.435 --> 35:05.812
[man] Fire!

35:07.063 --> 35:08.731
Fire over there!

35:09.857 --> 35:11.067
Fire!

35:12.568 --> 35:13.736
Fire!

35:22.036 --> 35:23.913
[man] Bring more water here!

35:33.506 --> 35:34.715
[wailing]

35:35.800 --> 35:36.759
[man 2] It's breaking!

35:39.345 --> 35:40.263
It's no use!

35:48.104 --> 35:50.398
[wailing, gasping]

35:58.322 --> 36:00.116
[pants]

36:11.502 --> 36:12.587
The food.

36:13.045 --> 36:15.339
Were you able to save
any of the food inside?

36:15.923 --> 36:16.883
No, sir. I'm sorry.

36:20.803 --> 36:22.847
This was your watch! What were you doing?

36:23.514 --> 36:25.224
How could you let this happen
on your guard?

36:25.308 --> 36:26.684
We don't know, sir.

36:26.767 --> 36:28.477
All of a sudden,
there was an explosion, and--

36:28.561 --> 36:29.645
You fool!

36:31.314 --> 36:33.858
Do you know how valuable
that warehouse was?

36:33.941 --> 36:37.111
The lives of everyone here
depended on the food that was inside!

36:37.195 --> 36:38.237
[guard] I'm sorry.

36:38.905 --> 36:39.739
It's all my fault.

36:40.531 --> 36:42.116
- [crowd gasping]
- You should die!

36:42.200 --> 36:43.326
[man] It was me!

36:46.537 --> 36:47.914
I left it alone.

36:50.625 --> 36:53.252
[indistinct chatter]

36:54.921 --> 36:55.796
I did this.

36:58.382 --> 36:59.383
The fault...

37:02.094 --> 37:03.346
it's mine.

37:05.681 --> 37:07.934
I couldn't let my child starve to death,

37:08.893 --> 37:11.062
so I just tried to take some rice.

37:12.188 --> 37:14.065
[tearfully]
I didn't know this would happen.

37:14.857 --> 37:16.192
I dropped my lamp.

37:16.692 --> 37:18.361
I dropped it by accident.

37:18.444 --> 37:20.529
[sobs]

37:22.740 --> 37:24.283
I'm sorry!

37:27.328 --> 37:28.162
Do it.

37:29.705 --> 37:31.666
Just kill me.
[sobs]

37:35.461 --> 37:37.463
[somber music]

37:41.175 --> 37:42.468
What does it matter?

37:43.761 --> 37:45.096
We're going to die.

37:48.057 --> 37:49.183
Whether we starve to death...

37:52.311 --> 37:54.397
or get eaten by those monsters,

37:56.482 --> 37:58.109
we're all going to die.

38:15.209 --> 38:19.714
MUNGYEONG SAEJAE

38:40.526 --> 38:41.527
[Seo-bi sighs]

38:42.486 --> 38:45.197
Do you really think you can use that
to stop this disease?

38:46.032 --> 38:49.994
There's always a way to stop it,
no matter how severe the disease is.

38:50.077 --> 38:51.746
And this one is no different.

38:52.997 --> 38:54.957
If I study this plant's properties,

38:55.082 --> 38:58.210
I am sure I can find a way
to put an end to this disease.

38:58.711 --> 39:00.755
As long as we stay in Mungyeong Saejae,

39:01.213 --> 39:02.798
we should be safe.

39:02.882 --> 39:05.593
[sighs heavily]

39:06.552 --> 39:09.430
There are still people alive
in the citadel of Sangju.

39:11.891 --> 39:13.601
We have to save those people.

39:15.311 --> 39:17.313
Right. His Highness...

39:18.898 --> 39:20.816
[Hak-ju] What is that in your hand?

39:20.900 --> 39:21.942
[Seo-bi gasps]

39:25.196 --> 39:26.989
[guard] Hand it over, now!

39:44.215 --> 39:46.092
Do you know what this plant is?

39:46.425 --> 39:47.551
[sighs]

39:53.557 --> 39:55.309
It brings the dead to life.

39:55.643 --> 39:57.228
It's called the resurrection plant.

39:58.896 --> 40:00.272
This plant's behind...

40:01.732 --> 40:03.359
It's behind this outbreak.

40:05.152 --> 40:07.196
And how do you know this?

40:07.279 --> 40:08.280
[gasps]

40:09.573 --> 40:12.535
I first learned of this
through this nurse.

40:15.663 --> 40:18.207
Go on, then. Tell them how you know.

40:18.999 --> 40:20.084
[breathing shakily]

40:24.004 --> 40:27.925
"The resurrection plant was used
to bring the dead King back to life.

40:29.218 --> 40:31.720
This plant is the cause of this disease."

40:33.347 --> 40:35.808
Is that what Lee Seung-hui told you?

40:36.517 --> 40:38.144
Oh, what do you mean by that?

40:39.270 --> 40:40.771
What do you mean... "The dead King"?

40:42.106 --> 40:44.567
[breathing shakily]
Please have mercy.

40:44.650 --> 40:47.153
The only reason I found that plant
is because read about it

40:47.236 --> 40:48.946
in his patient journal.

40:49.655 --> 40:51.740
You read his patient journal?

40:53.826 --> 40:55.536
Then you must also know...

40:57.455 --> 40:59.707
how to raise the dead back to life.

41:07.590 --> 41:10.843
"If you mash the resurrection plant,
put it on a needle,

41:10.926 --> 41:13.345
and insert it deep into the glabella,

41:13.596 --> 41:16.724
in two hours' time,
the dead will return to life.

41:16.807 --> 41:18.809
That's what he wrote in his journal.

41:26.317 --> 41:28.527
I will take that girl to Hanyang as well.

41:31.572 --> 41:32.865
Make preparations.

41:32.948 --> 41:34.116
[guard] Yes, my lord.

41:34.617 --> 41:36.952
Hanyang? When? What for?

41:42.750 --> 41:47.213
There is still unfinished... work to do.

41:48.923 --> 41:50.174
When it is done...

41:51.592 --> 41:54.678
I will return to Hanyang
and meet the future prince.

42:00.559 --> 42:03.687
SANGJU, LORD AHN HYEON'S RESIDENCE

42:04.605 --> 42:05.439
[Ann-hyeon] Wait.

42:06.232 --> 42:07.358
What did you say?

42:10.319 --> 42:11.987
I will go to Mungyeong Saejae.

42:12.696 --> 42:13.531
Your Highness.

42:14.240 --> 42:16.116
Those monsters are everywhere.

42:16.200 --> 42:17.993
Mungyeong Saejae
will be impossible to reach.

42:18.661 --> 42:20.412
To save our people, I must go.

42:21.580 --> 42:23.374
I will require your best men.

42:26.794 --> 42:27.920
[foreboding music]

42:39.265 --> 42:41.141
I will lead the way, Your Highness.

42:52.236 --> 42:53.070
Let's go.

43:16.260 --> 43:17.886
[snarling]

44:16.320 --> 44:19.615
[suspenseful music]

45:16.380 --> 45:18.382
[somber music]

45:41.739 --> 45:43.157
Extinguish your torches.

45:56.920 --> 45:59.298
[tense music]

46:06.722 --> 46:08.891
The north branch is very close
to the passageway.

46:08.974 --> 46:11.643
The monsters fear water,
so if we cross the river,

46:12.394 --> 46:14.313
we should be able to escape them.

46:15.397 --> 46:17.107
Even if you cross the north branch,

46:17.191 --> 46:19.359
Mungyeong Saejae
will not be easy to enter.

46:20.235 --> 46:21.862
The Five Armies will be
guarding the gates.

46:22.404 --> 46:24.656
The number of soldiers
has dropped to a mere tenth

46:24.740 --> 46:26.492
due to the war three years ago.

46:26.575 --> 46:29.703
There are 5,000 elite soldiers
in Hanyang alone.

46:30.245 --> 46:31.872
But even for Cho Hak-ju...

46:32.498 --> 46:34.792
it will be difficult
to send all those men.

46:36.043 --> 46:37.586
At most, the number...

46:38.086 --> 46:39.797
cannot be more than 2,500,

46:40.214 --> 46:42.132
less than half the available force.

46:42.216 --> 46:45.594
That is not many to guard
all the gates of Gyeongsang.

46:46.970 --> 46:48.347
They would be undermanned.

46:48.889 --> 46:50.015
I agree.

46:51.016 --> 46:52.976
If they are guarding every gate,

46:53.060 --> 46:55.020
Mungyeong Saejae could have no more...

46:55.729 --> 46:56.939
than 500 men.

46:57.272 --> 46:58.732
It would not be possible

46:58.816 --> 47:01.693
to guard all of Mungyeong Saejae's walls
with that number.

47:01.777 --> 47:05.280
The northwest section
of the first gate is built very high.

47:05.364 --> 47:07.991
Functionally, it requires little defense.

47:08.075 --> 47:10.369
The amount of men on guard would be few.

47:10.452 --> 47:12.329
WEST SIDE, SOUTH SIDE

47:12.412 --> 47:15.040
Well, then, once you're
in Mungyeong Saejae,

47:15.541 --> 47:17.167
what is Your Highness' plan?

47:23.757 --> 47:25.092
Cho Hak-ju...

47:27.177 --> 47:29.054
will die by my sword.

47:29.596 --> 47:32.057
For his shameless disregard
of the people,

47:32.140 --> 47:34.268
and for his traitorous attempt
to steal the throne,

47:34.977 --> 47:37.187
I will punish him and reclaim my place.

47:38.730 --> 47:42.025
I will end this disease
and save our people from starvation.

47:43.277 --> 47:44.736
And I will survive...

47:48.866 --> 47:50.701
and create a new world.

47:59.209 --> 48:01.211
[closing theme music]
